 1: Calculate the time head start of the first train\n\nThe first train leaves at 9:40, and the second train leaves at 10:15. We need to find the duration between these two times.\n\n*   From 9:40 to 10:00 is 20 minutes.\n*   From 10:00 to 10:15 is 15 minutes.\n*   Total head start time ($t_{head}$) = $20 + 15 = 35$ minutes.\n\nConvert this time into hours, as the speeds are given in km/h:\n$$ t_{head} = \\frac{35}{60} \\text{ hours} = \\frac{7}{12} \\text{ hours} $$\n\n### Step 2: Determine the distance the first train travels during the head start\n\nWhile the second train is waiting, the first train is already moving. We calculate the distance ($d_{lead}$) covered", "client": {"ttft_s": 0.4760024999995949, "decode_s": 1.9774104000025545, "total_s": 2.4536369999987073, "n_gen": 256, "n_chunks": 256, "tg": 128.95653830872467, "pp": 134.45307535160944}}
